1. How I Would Handle the Situation

Since all three things are important, I would stay calm and handle them based on urgency and impact.

First, I would handle the sales call. The potential client is already on the phone and is comparing other companies, so I would give them my full attention and try to book a consultation for today.

Next, I would handle the CEO's scheduling conflict. I would check the calendar, inform the CEO that there is already a demo at 3:30 PM, and contact the existing client to see if we can move the demo to another available time.

Then, I would handle the support issue. I would reply to the customer right away so they know their concern has been received, then send the issue to the technical team for urgent assistance.

I would keep notes of each task and set reminders for any follow-ups so nothing gets missed.

2. Inbound Sales Lead — Phone Response

“Absolutely, I’d be happy to help. I can provide the pricing information I have available and learn a little more about what you’re looking for. Since you’re making a decision soon, I can also check our schedule and book you for a consultation today with the right person who can answer your questions in more detail.”

I would be friendly and confident, but I wouldn't promise anything that I’m not authorized to offer. Before ending the call, I would confirm the meeting time and make sure I have the correct contact details.

