James

4. Message to the CEO

Hi [CEO Name], I noticed that the 3:30 PM slot already has a client demo scheduled. I’ll contact the client and work on moving the demo to the nearest available time so we can keep 3:30 PM available for the emergency meeting. I’ll update the calendar and confirm everything once it’s arranged.

Bonus Challenge
1. Message to the Executive

Hi [CEO Name], I noticed we’ve had a few calendar conflicts recently. For the rest of this week, I suggest that I monitor your calendar closely and approve any new bookings that would overlap with existing meetings. This should help prevent double-bookings and reduce last-minute schedule changes.

2. Simple Calendar SOP Rule

Before booking any meeting with an executive, the calendar must be checked first. If the requested time overlaps with an existing event, the meeting cannot be booked without approval from the executive or designated calendar manager.

How and Why I Work This Way

My main approach is to stay organized, communicate clearly, and deal with urgent matters first. I don't want to rush and make mistakes, so I make sure each task has a clear next step and follow up until it is completed.

This allows me to support the sales team, customers, and executives at the same time while making sure important tasks don't get forgotten.
